A property exposes getter and optionally setter logic using attribute-like syntax. This supports validation and computed attributes without changing the public interface. Syntax: @property
def value(self):
    return self._value

Explain the data flow and use: @property
def value(self):
    return self._value

class Result:
    def __init__(self, score):
        self.score = score
    @property
    def score(self):
        return self._score
    @score.setter
    def score(self, value):
        if not 0 <= value <= 100:
            raise ValueError("invalid")
        self._score = value
print(Result(89).score)

Suggested starting pattern: @property
def value(self):
    return self._value

